/** @mainpage %Qore kalman Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section kalmanintro kalman Module Introduction

    The \c kalman module provides Kalman filter bindings on top of
    <a href="https://eigen.tuxfamily.org">Eigen</a> for the
    <a href="https://docs.qore.org/current/lang/html/index.html">Qore programming language</a>.

    Kalman filters are the standard approach for denoising, tracking,
    sensor-fusing, and smoothing sequential noisy observations. Canonical
    applications:

    - <b>Navigation / tracking</b> — GPS/INS fusion, vehicle / pedestrian
      tracking, where noisy position measurements are smoothed against
      a motion model.
    - <b>Control systems</b> — state estimation for closed-loop controllers
      that must react to filtered state, not raw sensor noise.
    - <b>Industrial IoT</b> — sensor-signal denoising for predictive
      maintenance, anomaly detection.
    - <b>Finance</b> — smoothing noisy price series into trend estimates,
      volatility tracking.

    @section kalmanapi kalman Module API

    Main classes:
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::Matrix "Matrix" — dense matrix primitive
      (Eigen-backed); arithmetic, transpose, inverse, cholesky,
      determinant. Immutable — every operation returns a new matrix.
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::LinearFilter "LinearFilter" — standard Kalman
      filter (LKF) for linear Gaussian systems. Set F / H / Q / R /
      initial state, then call \c predict() / \c update() per step.
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::ExtendedFilter "ExtendedFilter" — extended
      Kalman filter (EKF) for non-linear dynamics or observations. The
      non-linear state-transition and measurement functions are supplied
      as Qore callbacks; the callback also returns the Jacobian.

    Standalone functions:
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::kalman_version() "kalman_version()" — module
      version string.
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::get_kalman_info() "get_kalman_info()" —
      structured version info.

    Pre-baked model factories (1.1+):
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::newConstantVelocity2D() "newConstantVelocity2D()" — one-call 2D CV filter (state:
      @c [x, y, vx, vy]).
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::newConstantAcceleration2D() "newConstantAcceleration2D()" — one-call 2D CA filter
      (state: @c [x, y, vx, vy, ax, ay]).
    - @ref Qore::Kalman::newGpsSmoother() "newGpsSmoother()" — 2D CV
      tuned for GPS smoothing, with @c sigma_gps_base parameterising
      the measurement noise floor. Our canonical business-use-case
      helper; replaces ~300 lines of hand-rolled scalar matrix
      arithmetic with a single call.

    @section kalmanthread Thread safety

    @ref Qore::Kalman::Matrix "Matrix" is immutable after construction
    — every method returns a new matrix rather than mutating the
    receiver. Sharing a @c Matrix across threads is safe.

    Filter objects (@ref Qore::Kalman::LinearFilter "LinearFilter",
    @ref Qore::Kalman::ExtendedFilter "ExtendedFilter") hold
    mutable state (the current state vector and covariance matrix)
    and must <b>not</b> be shared across threads without external
    locking. Typical usage is one filter per tracked object (per
    vehicle, per sensor, per stream) — no concurrency issue then.

    @section kalmandocumentation Documentation

    - @subpage kalmancookbook
    - @subpage kalmanrelease
*/
